…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtSpeak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, If any man's wife go aside, and commit a trespass against him,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾and a man lie with her carnally, and it be hid from the eyes of her husband, and be kept close, and she be defiled, and there be no witness against her, neither she be taken with the manner;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿and the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be defiled: or if the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be not defiled;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ then shall the man bring his wife unto the priest, and he shall bring her offering for her, the tenth part of an ephah of barley meal; he shall pour no oil upon it, nor put frankincense thereon; for it is an offering of jealousy, an offering of memorial, bringing iniquity to remembrance.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAAnd the priest shall bring her near, and set her before the LORD:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£and the priest shall take holy water in an earthen vessel; and of the dust that is in the floor of the tabernacle the priest shall take, and put it into the water:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙïand the priest shall set the woman before the LORD, and uncover the woman's head, and put the offering of memorial in her hands, which is the jealousy offering: and the priest shall have in his hand the bitter water that causeth the curse:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙòand the priest shall charge her by an oath, and say unto the woman, If no man have lain with thee, and if thou hast not gone aside to uncleanness with another instead of thy husband, be thou free from this bitter water that causeth the curse:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbut if thou hast gone aside to another instead of thy husband, and if thou be defiled, and some man have lain with thee beside thine husband:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙãthen the priest shall charge the woman with an oath of cursing, and the priest shall say unto the woman, The LORD make thee a curse and an oath among thy people, when the LORD doth make thy thigh to rot, and thy belly to swell;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–and this water that causeth the curse shall go into thy bowels, to make thy belly to swell, and thy thigh to rot: And the woman shall say, Amen, amen.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdAnd the priest shall write these curses in a book, and he shall blot them out with the bitter water:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœand he shall cause the woman to drink the bitter water that causeth the curse: and the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her, and become bitter.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Then the priest shall take the jealousy offering out of the woman's hand, and shall wave the offering before the LORD, and offer it upon the altar:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤and the priest shall take an handful of the offering, even the memorial thereof, and burn it upon the altar, and afterward shall cause the woman to drink the water.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚBAnd when he hath made her to drink the water, then it shall come to pass, that, if she be defiled, and have done trespass against her husband, that the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her, and become bitter, and her belly shall swell, and her thigh shall rot: and the woman shall be a curse among her people.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And if the woman be not defiled, but be clean; then she shall be free, and shall conceive seed.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiThis is the law of jealousies, when a wife goeth aside to another instead of her husband, and is defiled;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­or when the spirit of jealousy cometh upon him, and he be jealous over his wife, and shall set the woman before the LORD, and the priest shall execute upon her all this law.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVThen shall the man be guiltless from iniquity, and this woman shall bear her iniquity.¦layout ªlast_verse